107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (Early diagnosis of neurological disorders remains a major challenge in modern healthcare. Traditional diagnostic approaches often rely on clinical neurological examinations, imaging techniques such as MRI or CT scans, and specialized neurological assessments. While these methods are effective, they can be expensive, time-consuming, and sometimes inaccessible in low-resource settings.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
108 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (In many neurodegenerative diseases, the symptoms develop gradually over time. As a result, patients may not receive a diagnosis until the disease has already progressed to a more advanced stage. Early detection is critical because it allows clinicians to initiate therapeutic interventions earlier, potentially slowing disease progression and improving patient quality of life.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
109 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (Speech abnormalities often appear during the early stages of neurological disorders. However, these abnormalities may be subtle and difficult to detect through subjective clinical evaluation alone. Recent studies suggest that computational analysis of speech signals using machine learning techniques can identify these subtle changes with high accuracy.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
110 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (Despite the promising results reported in the literature, there is still a need for accessible and efficient systems capable of performing automated voice-based neurological screening.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
111 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 60 0 R
/E (This project aims to address this gap by developing a computational framework capable of analyzing voice signals and predicting the likelihood of neurological disorders.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
